## Graphical abstract
Halogen bonding induced aqueously stable $\mathbf{CsPbBr_{3}/M O F s}$ -Derived $\bf C o3O_{4}/N$ -doped-C heterostructure for high-performance photoelectrochemical water oxidation
A novel strategy of modifying $\mathrm{Cs}\mathrm{Pb}{\mathrm{Br}}_{3}$ with MOFs-derived $\mathrm{Co_{3}O_{4}/N}$ -doped-C framework for constructing heterostructured photoanode for high performance photoelectrochemical water oxidation is demonstrated. The resultant photoanode represents largely improved carrier transport, photoelectrocatalysis performance with satisfactory aqueous stability.
